# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# We have problems to decide whether a variation is A43 or A45.
# First example: ---------------------
# A43 1.d4 c5 2.d5 Nf6 3.Bg5 Qb6 4.Nc3
# A45 1.d4 Nf6 2.Bg5 c5 3.d5 Qb6 4.Nc3
# Second example: --------------------
# A43: 1.d4 c5 2.d5 d6 3.e4 Nf6 4.Nc3
# A45: 1.d4 Nf6 2.Nc3 c5 3.d5 d6 4.e4
# We decide that variations with ...c5 d5 should belong to Benoni (A43).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Moreover we have problems to decide whether a variation id A43 or A48.
# Example: ----------------------------------
# A43 1.d4 c5 2.d5 d6 3.e4 Nf6 4.Nc3 g6 5.Nf3
# A48 1.d4 Nf6 2.Nf3 g6 3.Nc3 c5 4.d5 d6 5.e4
# 1. Scid assigns A43 in both cases
# 2. CB assigns A43 in both cases, but 1.d4 Nf6 2.Nf3 g6 3.Nc3 c5 4.d5 d6 is A43
# 3. chesstempo assigns mostly A43
# We decide that a variation with ...c5 d5 should belong to Benoni (A43).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
